<title>BELGIUM: Electrafina sees 1997 gain from U.S. sale.</title>
<headline>Electrafina sees 1997 gain from U.S. sale.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-01-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Belgian holding company Electrafina said on Friday it would book a capital gain of more than four billion Belgian francs in its 1997 accounts from an oil asset sale by 100 percent subsidiary  American Cometra to New York Stock Exchange-listed Lomak Petroleum.</p>
<p>&quot;(The sale) will also have the effect of adding 150 francs to the earnings per share of the company,&quot; Electrafina said in a statement.</p>
<p>Electrafina said the sale concerned oil and gas reserves held by Cometra in Texas and the Gulf of Mexico, as well as associated transport and processing facilities.</p>
<p>The $400 million sale should be completed at the end of February, the company said.</p>
<p>-- Nick Antonovics, Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6817, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
